# Project memory

Memory lives in `.cursor/memory/` inside this repo. It is not `~/.shokunin`, not ChromaDB, and not a filesystem MCP on the home directory. This machine has Python 3.9 and no Homebrew 3.11+, so recall is keyword search over local JSONL.

## Session start

1. Read `.cursor/memory/index.md`
2. Run `python3 scripts/shokunin-memory.py search "<current task>"` or `sessions --limit 5`
3. Treat hits as claims. Verify file paths before acting
4. Do not announce a memory dump unless something changes the task

## During work

Save only durable facts, not every turn:

```bash
python3 scripts/shokunin-memory.py save --type decision --text "..."
python3 scripts/shokunin-memory.py save --type preference --text "..."
python3 scripts/shokunin-memory.py save --type checkpoint --text "..."
```

Types: `decision`, `file`, `command`, `preference`, `checkpoint`, `session_end`, `general`.

Never store secrets, `.env` values, tokens, or account passwords.

## Session end

```bash
python3 scripts/shokunin-memory.py end --text "Decisions: ... Files: ... Next: ..."
python3 scripts/shokunin-memory.py index
```

If the `shokunin-memory` MCP server is connected, use those tools instead of the CLI. Same store either way.
